EN:
A new week has just begun!{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
If I do my job right, we'll get
a slew of visitors by tomorrow!

ES:
¡Comienza una nueva semana!{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
Tengo que trabajar duro si quiero
que mañana vengan muchos clientes.

FR:
C'est le début de la semaine !{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
Demain, je me surpasserai pour
attirer plus de visiteurs !

IT:
È cominciata una nuova settimana!{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
Se faccio bene il mio lavoro, entro
domani avremo moltissimi visitatori!

DE:
Eine neue Woche beginnt!{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
Wenn ich meinen Job richtig mache,
haben wir in Windeseile viele Gäste!

EN:
Starting tomorrow, we do battle
with the remainder of the week.{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
That's why I'm relaxing today!

FR:
On approche de la fin de la semaine.{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
J'essaye de me détendre un peu
pour attaquer la journée de demain.

IT:
Da domani fino alla fine della
settimana ci sarà tantissimo lavoro.{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
Per questo oggi mi riposo un po'!

EN:
Tomorrow is Friday!{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}} My heavens,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
it's easy to lose track of what day
it is when you work so much.

ES:
¡Mañana es viernes!{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}} Madre mía,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
con tanto trabajo ya no sé ni en
qué día vivo.

FR:
Demain, c'est vendredi ! {{TAG:0007:0001:}}On perd
facilement la notion du temps {{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
quand on travaille sans relâche !

IT:
Domani è già venerdì!{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}} Ah!{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
Quando si lavora così tanto,
è facile dimenticare che giorno è.

DE:
Morgen ist Freitag!{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}} Du liebe Zeit,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
wie schnell doch die Woche
vergeht, wenn man so viel arbeitet!

TRANSLATION:
Yarın cuma! Çok{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}} çalışınca{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
haftanın hangi günü olduğunu
unutmak ne kadar kolay.

IT:
Questa settimana è volata{{TAG:0007:0000:05000000}}.{{TAG:0007:0000:05000000}}.{{TAG:0007:0000:05000000}}.{{TAG:0007:0000:05000000}}{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
Eppure{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}} ho ancora un sacco
di lavoro da sbrigare domani!
Al Quartiere Sbirciacase c'è sempre
un sacco da fare nel fine settimana.{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
Niente relax, nemmeno nel weekend!

Domani è domenica.{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
Spero che al Quartiere Sbirciacase
arrivino più visitatori del solito.

DE:
Morgen fängt eine neue Woche an!{{TAG:0007:0001:}}
Und auch da sollten wir immer
unser Bestes geben!

EN:
Whenever I'm with my twin sister,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
she always talks on and on about
everyone who lives in {{TAG:0005:0005:}}.
{{TAG:0003:0001:}}It makes me feel like I know every
person in town on a deeper level,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
even if we haven't spoken much.
{{TAG:0003:0000:}}I'm sure my sister has her flaws,{{TAG:0007:0000:0A000000}}
but I know she's well taken care
of with this town's happy spirit!
